      "math_academy_id": "e-14176",
      "problem": "If $f(x)$ is given by the table shown below, what are its roots?\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $5$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given table, we see that $f(-2)=0$ and $f(1)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=-2$ and $x=1.$",
